\": null, \"evidence\": \"Card \\\"Professional Resume\\\": category badge Resume, scenario badge Business, author Sarah Chen, 1,250 uses, Updated 2024-12-01, plus title and description.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Built-in Markdown resume preview: h1/h2/h3 headings, strong (\\\"Software Engineer\\\", \\\"B.S. Computer Science\\\"), emphasis (\\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\"), a separator (hr), and paragraph line breaks all rendered; no unresolved {{placeholders}} remain.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category=Resume → \\\"Showing 1 of 6\\\", only Professional Resume. Scenario=Academic → \\\"Showing 1 of 6\\\", only Academic Research Summary. Sorts verified against data: Most Popular (1250→340 uses), Recently Updated (2024-12-05→2024-09-30), Oldest First (createdAt 2024-01-08→2024-05-12), Alphabetical (Academic…→Weekly…).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Search is exact-substring only; no typo tolerance or fuzzy matching\", \"actual\": \"Single-character typos of existing keywords all yield \\\"Showing 0 of 6 templates\\\" / \\\"No templates found\\\" with no suggestions: \\\"resmue\\\", \\\"resme\\\", \\\"resune\\\", \\\"reusme\\\" (vs \\\"Resume\\\"), \\\"meting\\\", \\\"meetng\\\" (vs \\\"Meeting\\\"), \\\"weekli\\\" (vs \\\"Weekly\\\"). Correct spelling \\\"resu\\\" matches fine, confirming only literal substring matching is implemented.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Heart on Professional Resume and Meeting Minutes added both (Favorites badge 1→2, storage [\\\"1\\\",\\\"3\\\"]); header \\\"Favorites\\\" toggle opened a favorites-only list showing exactly those 2. Unfavoriting Meeting Minutes removed it (badge → 1, list → only Professional Resume).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In favorites-only view (2 favorites), search \\\"professional\\\" returned only the favorited \\\"Professional Resume\\\" (not the non-favorited \\\"Professional Email\\\"); category filter = Meeting Minutes returned only \\\"Meeting Minutes\\\". Both stayed scoped to favorites.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"Copy to Clipboard\\\" wrote raw Markdown (template's declared format) captured via patched clipboard.writeText: \\\"# Jane Doe\\\\n\\\\n**Software Engineer** | ... ## Skills\\\\nJavaScript, React, Node.js\\\", and toast \\\"Copied to clipboard! The generated content has been copied.\\\" appeared.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-28\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After reloading http://localhost:6089/, the library shows \\\"Showing 8 of 8\\\" including both custom templates (\\\"QA Daily Standup\\\", \\\"QA Plain Note\\\"). The Favorites badge still reads 1 and the favorites-only view shows \\\"Professional Resume\\\" with a filled heart (fill-current), persisted via localStorage.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Declared-format field (Email) accepts invalid value with no validation\", \"actual\": \"Email field (placeholder john@example.com) was filled with \\\"not-an-email\\\". No error was shown, the \\\"Required fields missing\\\" banner cleared, the Preview Result tab became enabled, and the preview rendered the line \\\"Software Engineer | not-an-email | +1 555 010 2030\\\".\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting the fully empty form left the dialog open and library at 6 (no template created). Filling title, author, description and content but defining zero fields was also blocked (library still 6). Submission only succeeded once ≥1 field was defined. Note: blocking is silent