    "content": "All 26 checklist items have been tested and recorded — **21 PASS, 5 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe core template-library experience is solid: browsing, card metadata, template selection, field filling, preview generation, Markdown/plain-text rendering, clipboard copy, filtering, sorting, favorites, and localStorage persistence all work as specified, with live updates and no reloads.\n\n**The 5 failures cluster around input validation:**\n\n1. **CS-14 — No format validation.** The Email field accepted `not-an-email`; the preview enabled and rendered the invalid value verbatim.\n\n2. **CS-17 — Incomplete special-character filtering.** The app blocks `< > { } [ ] \\ | ` `` but not `*`, `#`, `-`. Entering `## Evil **Bold** --- Heading` produced `<h1>## Evil <strong>Bold</strong> --- Heading</h1>`, injecting a `<strong>` element not present in the template.\n\n3. **CS-27 — No field↔placeholder mapping validation**, in *both* directions: a template submitted with a declared `{{team_name}}` field but no placeholder in its content, and another with `{{ticket_id}}` in content but no declared field — the latter renders the literal unresolved `{{ticket_id}}` in its preview.\n\n4. **CS-29 — Duplicate labels collide.** Two fields labeled \"Name\" were both accepted and assigned the same id `name`. Typing into one input simultaneously filled the other, so they cannot be filled independently (also triggered React duplicate-key console errors).\n\n5. **FT-10 — Search has no typo tolerance.** Despite the fuzzy-matching requirement, search is literal substring only. Seven typo variants (`resmue`, `resme`, `resune`, `reusme`, `meting`, `meetng`, `weekli`) all returned \"No templates found\" with zero suggestions, while correctly-spelled `resu` matched fine.\n\nOne additional observation worth noting (recorded but not failed): **CS-16 blocks invalid submissions silently** — clicking \"Submit Template\" on an empty or incomplete form does nothing at all, with no inline error or toast, leaving users without an explanation."
  }
}
